From: JCOW414 diagnostic build
Subject: [PATCH] leds: netdev: skip unnamed hardware-control devices

A PHY-backed LED can become visible before the associated network device
has a name. Avoid passing that NULL name to strlen during trigger activation;
leave hardware control disabled and complete software-trigger setup instead.

--- a/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c
@@ -715,7 +715,8 @@ static int netdev_trig_activate(struct led_classdev *led_cdev)
 	 */
 	if (supports_hw_control(led_cdev)) {
 		dev = led_cdev->hw_control_get_device(led_cdev);
-		if (dev) {
+		/* The PHY may precede netdev registration during startup. */
+		if (dev && dev_name(dev)) {
 			const char *name = dev_name(dev);
 
 			trigger_data->hw_control = true;
